gr=dict(t='Grammar – Compound words, Palindromes, Present Perfect', p=[
 'Compound word: two words joined to make a new word with a new meaning.',
 'Hyphenated: Cat’s-food-Man, check-in, well-bred | Open: bird language, sailor song, plough horse | Closed: flowerpots, teatime, windowsill.',
 'Palindrome: a word or sentence that reads the same backwards – level, radar, Malayalam, “Step on no pets”.',
 'Present continuous: is/am/are + V-ing – He is asking you a question.',
 'Present perfect: has/have + V3 (past participle) – It has stopped raining.',
 'Use the present perfect for 1) a recently completed action, 2) an action that started in the past and is still relevant, 3) when the action matters, not the time.',
 'V3 forms: learn–learnt, treat–treated, teach–taught, write–written, bring–brought, become–become.']),
